Subject: Cantor Faculty Deliberation Runtime

Description: The provider-independent boundary by which Cantor compiles, selects, loads, runs, validates, and coordinates SOP faculty programs as genuine bounded participants in checkpointed inference deliberation.

& [FacultyProgram] is a compiled attention and inference behavior
  + [faculty_identity] is Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Planner, Weaver, or another admitted bounded faculty
  + [source_contract] is the signed verbose SOP authority from which the program is compiled
  + [purpose] is the exact contribution the faculty is intended to make
  + [field] is the kind of subject identity the faculty observes
  + [boundary] is the distinctions the faculty must preserve
  + [activation_predicate] is the typed subject, state, consequence, uncertainty, conflict, or request condition that requires the faculty
  + [attention_program] is focus, hold, widen, narrow, admit, exclude, preserve, pull, peek, return, and related attention transforms
  + [inference_program] is questions, comparisons, derivations, challenges, alternatives, tests, and reconciliation obligations
  + [transformation_contract] is permitted input-to-output semantic changes
  + [gate_set] is evidence, Honesty, Security, authority, boundary, consequence, and faculty-specific validation
  + [input_schema] is the typed context the activation may observe
  + [output_schema] is the required judgment, proposal, objection, residual, ledger, and proof shape
  + [stop_contract] is fulfilled, insufficient_evidence, conflict, fault, budget, yield, or refusal
  + [program_digest] is the compiled identity bound to source, compiler, schema, and policy versions
  = must: compile from signed verbose authority through one semantic intermediate representation
  = must: remain inspectable and expandable from compact projection to authoritative meaning
  - never: grant external effect authority merely because a faculty program was activated

& [CantorFacultyRuntime] is the faculty compiler and deliberation conductor
  + [compile] is transform admitted faculty SOP into validated FacultyProgram records
  + [admit] is verify source signature, digest, schema, dependencies, and policy compatibility
  + [route] is match active subject state against activation predicates
  + [compose] is assemble the minimum materially sufficient faculty set for the purpose and consequence
  + [project] is load each program's attention and inference frame into its assigned provider context
  + [dispatch] is start or continue a bounded FacultyActivation
  + [validate] is check each return against program, evidence, authority, and anti-enchantment gates
  + [coordinate] is pass validated returns to Observer for reconciliation and next-step selection
  + [account] is preserve activation, frame, provider, output, objection, decision, and proof lineage
  = must: make faculty selection and omission inspectable
  = must: use consequence-sensitive activation rather than loading every faculty at full verbosity on every pass
  = must: preserve a faculty's dissent and residual uncertainty through Observer review
  - never: preselect a faculty output or suppress a valid objection to create deliberation theater

& [FacultyActivation] is one bounded execution of one FacultyProgram
  + [activation_uuid] is immutable invocation identity
  + [program_digest] is the exact FacultyProgram version
  + [subject_snapshot] is the signed or digest-bound subject state observed
  + [purpose_binding] is why this faculty is active now
  + [context_projection] is the bounded information supplied to the provider
  + [provider_binding] is model, deterministic evaluator, human, or other admitted reasoning implementation
  + [budget] is token, time, traversal, tool, recursion, and retry limit
  + [return] is the structured faculty output and ledger
  + [validation] is accepted, qualified, rejected, faulted, or unresolved
  = must: identify the information unavailable to the activation
  = must: return through Observer rather than committing an exterior effect

& [DeliberationParticipation] is the standard for real faculty participation
  + [independent_question] is the faculty receives a purpose-specific question not a demanded conclusion
  + [epistemic_opportunity] is the faculty can inspect evidence, raise counterevidence, disagree, qualify, refuse, or request more context
  + [causal_consequence] is a valid return can alter the candidate conclusion, activate another faculty, block an effect, or preserve an unresolved frontier
  + [addressed_objection] is Observer must accept, answer, qualify, escalate, or preserve every material objection
  + [trace] is the actual contribution and its effect on the deliberation path remain inspectable
  = must: preserve disagreement until evidence or explicit policy resolves it
  = must: distinguish a generated faculty-styled monologue from a causally effective faculty activation
  - never: call decorative role-play deliberation
  - never: force consensus as the price of returning a valid faculty result

& [FacultyExecutionMode] is the supported range of participation isolation
  + [inline_role_pass] is one provider performs sequential faculty passes in one controlled job
  + [isolated_context_job] is each faculty receives a separate context and returns through Cantor
  + [independent_provider_job] is faculties run on different models, providers, or hosts
  + [deterministic_faculty] is a non-model evaluator performs a fully specified faculty operation
  + [hybrid_mode] is deterministic gates and model judgments cooperate under the same program contract
  = must: label the execution mode and its independence limits
  = must: treat same-model role separation as useful perspective structure rather than proof of independent judgment
  = should: use isolated or diverse providers when correlated failure materially matters

& [FacultyAgentBoundary] is the distinction between a deliberation participant and commissioned agency
  + [logical_faculty_participant] is a FacultyActivation whose return can affect inference
  + [faculty_job_agent] is an isolated provider job with faculty identity, bounded input, return contract, and lifecycle
  + [Shaliach] is a separately commissioned agent acting for a principal under effect authority
  = may: call an isolated FacultyActivation an SOP-based deliberation agent when its identity and causal contribution are explicit
  = must: state that faculty-agent status does not imply consciousness, independent will, or exterior effect authority
  = must: require a CommissionContract and EffectBroker for a faculty-bearing runtime to act as Shaliach

& [CheckpointedFacultyCycle] is the provider-independent execution sequence
  + [step_1_observe] is Cantor binds purpose, subject snapshot, consequence, authority, and unresolved state
  + [step_2_route] is activation predicates propose the materially sufficient faculty set
  + [step_3_frame] is Cantor compiles or retrieves each signed FacultyProgram and creates context projections
  + [step_4_infer] is providers execute faculty passes and return structured judgments, objections, and ledgers
  + [step_5_validate] is Cantor applies schema, evidence, Honesty, Security, authority, and AntiEnchantment gates
  + [step_6_reconcile] is Observer compares returns, preserves differences, and determines the next bounded transition
  + [step_7_continue] is Cantor projects the reconciled state into the next inference checkpoint when required
  + [step_8_account] is Scribe preserves frames, outputs, decisions, residuals, digests, and proof
  = must: treat model calls and tool calls as explicit checkpoints
  - never: claim access to or mutation of inaccessible hidden attention state

& [RuntimeBoundary] is the separation of responsibilities
  + [Cantor] owns signed faculty compilation, routing, projection, validation, coordination state, and proof
  + [inference_provider] owns token inference or other reasoning execution
  + [Observer] owns reconciliation under the compiled governance program
  + [EffectBroker] owns authorized exterior action commitment
  + [Shaliach] owns the commissioned lifecycle when delegated agency exists
  = must: allow provider replacement without changing FacultyProgram semantics
  = must: validate every provider return as untrusted candidate material

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable faculty-runtime collection
  + [CFD-001] is compile faculty purposes, boundaries, transforms, gates, and return contracts into inspectable FacultyProgram records
  + [CFD-002] is activate faculties from typed conditions over the current subject and purpose
  + [CFD-003] is run faculty patterns through provider-independent checkpointed inference
  + [CFD-004] is require causally effective outputs, answerable objections, and preserved disagreement for real deliberation
  + [CFD-005] is support inline, isolated, independent-provider, deterministic, and hybrid execution modes
  + [CFD-006] is disclose correlated-failure and independence limits
  + [CFD-007] is distinguish faculty deliberation agents from commissioned Shaliach agency
  + [CFD-008] is return all specialist results through Observer and all effects through authorized gates
  + [CFD-009] is apply the Truthful Observation Frame and AntiEnchantmentInvariant to every activation

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the faculty-runtime justification record
  + [fold_1_subject] is Cantor as the engine that activates compiled faculty intentions inside inference deliberation
  + [fold_2_boundary] is observable context projection and checkpointed provider calls inside; hidden-state mutation, fabricated independence, and uncommissioned effects outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is FacultyProgram, activation predicate, FacultyActivation, provider binding, return, objection, reconciliation, and proof
  + [fold_4_governance] is signed compilation, minimum sufficient activation, Observer return, anti-enchantment validation, effect separation, and mode disclosure
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is observe, route, frame, infer, validate, reconcile, continue, and account
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is deliberation theater, forced consensus, correlated failure, context starvation, output suppression, authority escalation, and hidden-state overclaim
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is runtime architecture formed while implementation remains parked behind the bounded Cantor core gate

